  "pinAndProducerReview": "The operator captures the real publisher key at workspace creation before export and writes a signed peer record. Actual export/verify/import functions are used with no router, producer, trust-admission, archive or filesystem mock. Outer packages are integrity-valid, admitted and trusted with no overrides before destination links are introduced.",
  "destinationProof": "Normal recipient commits the complete signed package. Each static inbox/publisher/federation-root link returns a successful import instead of refusing and writes five copied files beyond the governed recipient boundary. Nine new rows for inbox/federation-root and eight for publisher include exact envelope, publisher-public-key and transparency-root hashes. Existing sentinel names/bytes/inode/link metadata remain equal; there is no claim that the sentinel content was overwritten.",
  "snapshotInterpretation": "Recipient lstat snapshots do not follow directory links and stay unchanged in all three REDs. The separate outside-target snapshots expose actual redirected writes. This distinction is preserved rather than treating the unchanged recipient alone as no-effects proof.",
